a funeral is under way for a police  officer in Italy allegedly murdered by  two American teenagers Mario Churchill  Arreaga was stabbed to death Friday in  Rome the two teens could both face life  in prison if convicted Seth Doane is  outside Naples Italy where mourners are  paying their respects to the officer  Seth what's the mood there mourners have  filled the streets here and only adding  to the emotion of this day is that the  officer who was killed was married in  this very same church just about a month  and a half ago the church was not big  enough for the crowd gathered today for  the funeral of Mario Churchill Arreaga a  vice brigadier in Italy's Carabinieri  Police Force my friend Mario was a good  person town mayor said he dedicated his  life to the service of the weakest  church eller Drago was stabbed to death  on a Rome Street an Italian law  enforcement says the two American  teenagers Finnegan Lee elder and Gabriel  Christian Natale orth confessed to being  involved this all started early Friday  morning when Italian police say the  Americans stole a backpack belonging to  an Italian man which included his cell  phone the man called the phone and the  Americans demanded a gram of cocaine and  a hundred euros to give the bag back  they set up a meeting point here and the  Italian man tipped off the Carabinieri  elder pulled out a knife according to  the arrest warrant and stabbed the  officer multiple times  Natalia orth says he did not see the  knife but in Italy someone can be  charged for murder if they were involved  even if they didn't carry out the  killing the pair had been schoolmates in  the Bay Area where teachers and students  have said they were troubled and had  disciplinary issues a picture of Natalia  you're blindfolded in the Carabinieri  station triggered questions about the  treatment of the teens though Rome's  Attorney General says the interrogation  was free of duress there is no place in  any criminal justice system for a  suspect to be blindfolded  that image of the blindfold is already  drawing comparisons to the case of  Amanda Knox who says she was mistreated  by Italian police during questioning  this case is likely to stretch on for  years CBS News has reached out to both  families and on Sunday the elder family  issued a statement which said they had  not had contact with their son since  Friday that they had been in touch with  the US State Department which had not  had access to him Michelle all right  Seth Doane in Italy thank you
 

